Sackar Atlas is a public data project by Anna Roberts.

It uses AI tools to synthesise data from public documents, such as the [Special Commission of Inquiry into LGBTIQ hate crimes report](https://www.nsw.gov.au/departments-and-agencies/cabinet-office/resources/special-commissions-of-inquiry/lgbtiq-hate-crimes) and the ACON [In Pursuit of Truth & Justice: Documenting Gay and Transgender Prejudice Killings in NSW in the Late 20th Century report](https://www.aconhealth.org.au/report_into_historic_gay_hate_murders_calls_for_justice_and_healing). The aim is to create a accessible record of this horrifying period of Sydney history and make the connections between cases, locations, and people in a way 3,000-page PDFs cannot.

The site is designed for community organisations, journalists, researchers, and the general public to use freely. [Source code on GitHub](https://github.com/bitsloppy/sackar-atlas)
